\section{Experimental Setup}
\label{sec:setup}

\subsection{Tasks and Datasets}
\label{sec:datasets}

We evaluate across three IE tasks with diverse schema characteristics (Table~\ref{tab:datasets}).

\paragraph{Named Entity Recognition.}
Few-NERD \citep{TODO-ding-fewnerd-2021} provides 66 fine-grained entity types organized under 8 coarse-grained domains (e.g., \textsc{Person}, \textsc{Location}, \textsc{Organization}), constituting a \emph{cross-domain} schema where types from different domains exhibit low semantic overlap.
We randomly sample 1{,}000 sentences from the test split.

\paragraph{Relation Extraction.}
FewRel \citep{TODO-han-fewrel-2018} defines 80 relation types sourced from Wikidata.
We construct 1{,}000 balanced instances (stratified across all 80 relations) from the combined training and validation splits.

\paragraph{Event Detection.}
MAVEN \citep{TODO-wang-maven-2020} defines 168 event types derived from FrameNet, forming a semantically homogeneous \emph{same-domain} schema.
We evaluate on the full validation set (710 documents, 18{,}904 trigger mentions).
The intentional inclusion of both cross-domain and same-domain schemas enables us to probe the boundary conditions of embedding-based confusability measures.

